{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c593","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07a5e-8204-7c61-b778-7e703c0d991a"},"sequence":292,"recorded_at":1780531400000579,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"b4a16fe6-9763-440b-bf19-bfec570b01d7"},"task_id":"b4a16fe6-9763-440b-bf19-bfec570b01d7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"b4a16fe6-9763-440b-bf19-bfec570b01d7","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_site_audit_test.go`.\n1|// Exercised-site audit for the terminal backend refusal arms.\n2|//\n3|// The failure this file exists to prevent: a declared, witnessed arm going\n4|// dead by construction while the whole suite stays green. Witnesses assert\n5|// the (code, detail) pair at a public entry; several arms share one pair\n6|// (62 of 184 witnessed arms share their clause with a sibling), so a\n7|// widened earlier guard swallows a later arm's inputs and the later\n8|// witness still passes through the sibling. That plant (P8:\n9|// CheckEntrypoint's first session parse widened to also compare, killing\n10|// the second parse and the comparison arms) left the derived set\n11|// byte-identical, the bijection at 210/210, and every witness green.\n12|//\n13|// The audit closes it the way provider and provhost already do: every\n14|// production refusal construction records its file:line at runtime\n15|// (through refuse/mismatchf/integrityFailure, armed by TestMain below),\n16|// and the post-run audit requires every derived non-bound line to have\n17|// fired at least once, and every fired line to be derived. A shadowed arm\n18|// never fires, so it reddens here as a derived site without an exercised\n19|// path. Bound arms (26 rows no input can reach) are exempt by their\n20|// declared rows, mapped to lines by TestDerivedSiteLinesAreExactlyRowed,\n21|// never by hand.\n22|//\n23|// Recording is off (nil hook) in production: construction is then a pure\n24|// allocation with zero behavior change.\n25|package terminalbackend\n26|\n27|import (\n28|\t\"flag\"\n29|\t\"fmt\"\n30|\t\"os\"\n31|\t\"runtime\"\n32|\t\"sort\"\n33|\t\"strconv\"\n34|\t\"strings\"\n35|\t\"sync\"\n36|\t\"testing\"\n37|\n38|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/invcore\"\n39|)\n40|\n41|// refusalSiteRecorder is the shared core's runtime direction: the\n42|// production file:line behind every refusal construction during the test\n43|// run, plus the wire codes those refusals carried. The hook is armed in\n44|// TestMain, so an aliased constructor still executes the funnel and\n45|// records its real production site: the runtime direction of the\n46|// alias-bypass union.\n47|var refusalSiteRecorder = invcore.NewSiteRecorder()\n48|\n49|func TestMain(main *testing.M) {\n50|\trecordRefusal = func(code, detail string) {\n51|\t\t// Skip counts the frames between Record and the production\n52|\t\t// site: the hook closure plus the funnel frame, matching the\n53|\t\t// provider/provhost swapped-constructor convention exactly\n54|\t\t// (pinned by TestRefusalSiteAttributionIsExact, not by reading).\n55|\t\trefusalSiteRecorder.Record(code, 2)\n56|\t}\n57|\tcode := main.Run()\n58|\tif code == 0 && fullPackageTestRun() {\n59|\t\tif failures := auditRefusalInventory(); len(failures) != 0 {\n60|\t\t\tfor _, failure := range failures {\n61|\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, failure)\n62|\t\t\t}\n63|\t\t\tcode = 1\n64|\t\t}\n65|\t}\n66|\tos.Exit(code)\n67|}\n68|\n69|func fullPackageTestRun() bool {\n70|\tselected := flag.Lookup(\"test.run\")\n71|\treturn selected == nil || selected.Value.String() == \"\"\n72|}\n73|\n74|// refusalAuditDomain is the captured in-band derivation the post-run\n75|// audit compares the exercised set against. It is captured by\n76|// TestDerivedSiteLinesAreExactlyRowed (which runs with a *testing.T and\n77|// can use the rich derivation) because TestMain has no *testing.T to\n78|// derive with. The audit fails closed when the domain is missing: a\n79|// scoped (-run) run never reaches the audit by fullPackageTestRun.\n80|type refusalAuditDomain struct {\n81|\tderived   map[string]struct{}\n82|\tbound     map[string]struct{}\n83|\twantCodes []string\n84|}\n85|\n86|var auditDomainMu sync.Mutex\n87|var capturedAuditDomain *refusalAuditDomain\n88|\n89|// TestDerivedSiteLinesAreExactlyRowed is the static half of site\n90|// attribution: every derived arm line resolves to exactly one declared\n91|// row and every declared row to exactly one derived line, and it captures\n92|// the domain the post-run exercised-site audit compares against. Bound\n93|// rows resolve to lines too: the exemption is row-derived, never listed.\n94|func TestDerivedSiteLinesAreExactlyRowed(t *testing.T) {\n95|\tt.Parallel()\n96|\n97|\tarms := deriveRefusalArms(t)\n98|\trows := declaredRows()\n99|\trowByKey := make(map[string]declaredRefusalArm, len(rows))\n100|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n101|\t\tkey := describeRow(row)\n102|\t\tif _, duplicate := rowByKey[key]; duplicate {\n103|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"declared row %s occurs twice; the mapping cannot attribute it\", key)\n104|\t\t}\n105|\t\trowByKey[key] = row\n106|\t}\n107|\tlineToRow := make(map[string]string)\n108|\trowToLine := make(map[string]string)\n109|\tfor _, arm := range arms {\n110|\t\t// The arm key space is occurrence-aware but line-free, and the\n111|\t\t// row key space is identical, so describeArm maps lines onto\n112|\t\t// rows through the shared identity without ever listing a line\n113|\t\t// by hand. (Line is not part of the key: describeArm never\n114|\t\t// reads it.)\n115|\t\tsite := arm.file + \":\" + strconv.Itoa(arm.line)\n116|\t\tkey := describeArm(arm)\n117|\t\trow, known := rowByKey[key]\n118|\t\tif !known {\n119|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"derived arm %s at %s resolves to no declared row\", key, site)\n120|\t\t\tcontinue\n121|\t\t}\n122|\t\trowKey := describeRow(row)\n123|\t\tif first, duplicate := lineToRow[site]; duplicate {\n124|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"derived line %s attributes rows %s and %s\", site, first, rowKey)\n125|\t\t\tcontinue\n126|\t\t}\n127|\t\tlineToRow[site] = rowKey\n128|\t\tif first, duplicate := rowToLine[rowKey]; duplicate {\n129|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"declared row %s resolves to lines %s and %s\", rowKey, first, site)\n130|\t\t\tcontinue\n131|\t\t}\n132|\t\trowToLine[rowKey] = site\n133|\t}\n134|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n135|\t\tif _, ok := rowToLine[describeRow(row)]; !ok {\n136|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"declared row %s resolves to no derived line\", describeRow(row))\n137|\t\t}\n138|\t}\n139|\tderived := make(map[string]struct{}, len(lineToRow))\n140|\tfor site := range lineToRow {\n141|\t\tderived[site] = struct{}{}\n142|\t}\n143|\tbound := make(map[string]struct{})\n144|\tfor site, rowKey := range lineToRow {\n145|\t\tif rowByKey[rowKey].bound != \"\" {\n146|\t\t\tbound[site] = struct{}{}\n147|\t\t}\n148|\t}\n149|\tsymbols := productionCodeSymbols(t)\n150|\tvar wantCodes []string\n151|\tfor symbol, wire := range symbols {\n152|\t\tif armlessCodes[symbol] {\n153|\t\t\tcontinue\n154|\t\t}\n155|\t\twantCodes = append(wantCodes, wire)\n156|\t}\n157|\tsort.Strings(wantCodes)\n158|\tauditDomainMu.Lock()\n159|\tcapturedAuditDomain = &refusalAuditDomain{derived: derived, bound: bound, wantCodes: wantCodes}\n160|\tauditDomainMu.Unlock()\n161|\tt.Logf(\"refusal-site audit domain: %d derived lines, %d bound-exempt, %d wire codes\",\n162|\t\tlen(derived), len(bound), len(wantCodes))\n163|}\n164|\n165|// auditRefusalInventory derives nothing: it compares the exercised\n166|// file:line set against the captured domain in both directions, plus the\n167|// closed wire-code set. A shadowed-dead arm never fires, so it fails here\n168|// as a derived site without an exercised path even though its pair still\n169|// refuses through its sibling and every witness stays green.\n170|func auditRefusalInventory() []string {\n171|\tauditDomainMu.Lock()\n172|\tdomain := capturedAuditDomain\n173|\tauditDomainMu.Unlock()\n174|\tif domain == nil || len(domain.derived) == 0 {\n175|\t\treturn []string{\"refusal-site audit: no captured audit domain; the mapping test did not run (full suite required)\"}\n176|\t}\n177|\tvar failures []string\n178|\texercised := refusalSiteRecorder.Sites()\n179|\tvar outside []string\n180|\tfor site := range exercised {\n181|\t\tif _, ok := domain.derived[site]; !ok {\n182|\t\t\toutside = append(outside, site)\n183|\t\t}\n184|\t}\n185|\tsort.Strings(outside)\n186|\tif len(outside) != 0 {\n187|\t\tfailures = append(failures, \"refusal-site audit: exercised refusal sites outside the derived inventory; the derivation is short: \"+strings.Join(outside, \", \"))\n188|\t}\n189|\tvar missing []string\n190|\tfor site := range domain.derived {\n191|\t\tif _, ok := domain.bound[site]; ok {\n192|\t\t\tcontinue\n193|\t\t}\n194|\t\tif _, ok := exercised[site]; !ok {\n195|\t\t\tmissing = append(missing, site)\n196|\t\t}\n197|\t}\n198|\tsort.Strings(missing)\n199|\tif len(missing) != 0 {\n200|\t\tfailures = append(failures, \"refusal-site audit: derived refusal sites without an exercised path (shadowed dead or unwitnessed): \"+strings.Join(missing, \", \"))\n201|\t}\n202|\tcodes := refusalSiteRecorder.Codes()\n203|\tif fmt.Sprintf(\"%v\", codes) != fmt.Sprintf(\"%v\", domain.wantCodes) {\n204|\t\tfailures = append(failures, fmt.Sprintf(\"refusal-site audit: observed refusal codes = %v, want closed set %v\", codes, domain.wantCodes))\n205|\t}\n206|\treturn failures\n207|}\n208|\n209|// TestRefusalSiteAttributionIsExact pins the recorder skip empirically:\n210|// a refusal built on the marked line must attribute to this file at that\n211|// line through each funnel.\n212|//\n213|// SEQUENTIAL BY DESIGN (no t.Parallel): it swaps the package hook, which\n214|// races with every parallel witness recording into the global recorder.\n215|// Sequential tests run exclusively before the parallel phase resumes, so\n216|// the swap is exclusive. Do not parallelize this test.\n217|func TestRefusalSiteAttributionIsExact(t *testing.T) {\n218|\tprobe := invcore.NewSiteRecorder()\n219|\tprevious := recordRefusal\n220|\trecordRefusal = func(code, detail string) {\n221|\t\tprobe.Record(code, 2)\n222|\t}\n223|\tdefer func() { recordRefusal = previous }()\n224|\n225|\t_, _, refuseLine, _ := runtime.Caller(0)\n226|\trefused := refuse(&Error{Code: CodeNotFound, Detail: \"attribution probe\"}) // want refuseLine+1\n227|\tif refused.Code != CodeNotFound || refused.Detail != \"attribution probe\" {\n228|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"refuse() = %+v, want the wrapped literal unchanged: recording never alters the refusal\", refused)\n229|\t}\n230|\t_, _, mismatchLine, _ := runtime.Caller(0)\n231|\tmismatched := mismatchf(\"attribution probe\") // want mismatchLine+1\n232|\tif mismatched.Code != CodeMismatch || mismatched.Detail != \"attribution probe\" {\n233|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"mismatchf() = %+v, want CodeMismatch at the static detail\", mismatched)\n234|\t}\n235|\t_, _, integrityLine, _ := runtime.Caller(0)\n236|\tintegrity := integrityFailure(\"attribution probe\") // want integrityLine+1\n237|\tif integrity.Code != CodeIntegrityFailure || integrity.Detail != \"attribution probe\" {\n238|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"integrityFailure() = %+v, want CodeIntegrityFailure at the static detail\", integrity)\n239|\t}\n240|\tsites := probe.Sites()\n241|\tfor _, want := range []string{\n242|\t\t\"refusal_site_audit_test.go:\" + strconv.Itoa(refuseLine+1),\n243|\t\t\"refusal_site_audit_test.go:\" + strconv.Itoa(mismatchLine+1),\n244|\t\t\"refusal_site_audit_test.go:\" + strconv.Itoa(integrityLine+1),\n245|\t} {\n246|\t\tif _, ok := sites[want]; !ok {\n247|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"attributed sites = %v, want %s recorded: the skip is wrong and the audit is blind\", sites, want)\n248|\t\t}\n249|\t}\n250|\tif len(sites) != 3 {\n251|\t\tt.Errorf(\"attributed sites = %v, want exactly the three probe sites\", sites)\n252|\t}\n253|}\n254|\n255|// TestRefuseFunnelRejectsAliases is the committed tb-level proof of the\n256|// alias-bypass union for the new funnel: a direct refuse call is\n257|// admitted, a var-bound refuse, a var-bound mismatchf (the P1 shape), and\n258|// an import-aliased errors.New (the P2 shape) all fail. Dropping refuse\n259|// from the watch list (N-tb-refuse) kills this test while the downstream\n260|// behav mask stays green.\n261|func TestRefuseFunnelRejectsAliases(t *testing.T) {\n262|\tt.Parallel()\n263|\n264|\tadmitted := `package terminalbackend\n265|func direct() *Error { return refuse(&Error{Code: CodeNotFound, Detail: \"x\"}) }\n266|`\n267|\tsyntax, fileSet, failure := invcore.ParseSource(\"direct.go\", []byte(admitted))\n268|\tif failure != \"\" {\n269|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse admitted source: %s\", failure)\n270|\t}\n271|\tif failures := invcore.AuditConstructorReferences(syntax, fileSet, \"direct.go\", refusalConstructorSpec()); len(failures) != 0 {\n272|\t\tt.Errorf(\"direct refuse call rejected: %v\", failures)\n273|\t}\n274|\trejected := map[string]string{\n275|\t\t\"var-bound refuse\": \"package terminalbackend\\nvar aliasedRefuse = refuse\\n\" +\n276|\t\t\t\"func indirect() *Error { return aliasedRefuse(&Error{Code: CodeNotFound, Detail: \\\"x\\\"}) }\\n\",\n277|\t\t\"var-bound mismatchf (P1)\": \"package terminalbackend\\nvar aliasedMismatch = mismatchf\\n\" +\n278|\t\t\t\"func indirect() *Error { return aliasedMismatch(\\\"x\\\") }\\n\",\n279|\t\t\"import-aliased errors.New (P2)\": \"package terminalbackend\\nimport errs \\\"errors\\\"\\n\" +\n280|\t\t\t\"var mintPlain = errs.New\\nfunc indirect() error { return mintPlain(\\\"x\\\") }\\n\",\n281|\t}\n282|\tfor name, source := range rejected {\n283|\t\tsyntax, fileSet, failure := invcore.ParseSource(\"plant.go\", []byte(source))\n284|\t\tif failure != \"\" {\n285|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s plant: %s\", name, failure)\n286|\t\t}\n287|\t\tfailures := invcore.AuditConstructorReferences(syntax, fileSet, \"plant.go\", refusalConstructorSpec())\n288|\t\tif len(failures) == 0 {\n289|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%s admitted: the alias bypasses attribution\", name)\n290|\t\t}\n291|\t}\n292|}"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c595","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07a5e-8204-7c61-b778-7e703c0d991a"},"sequence":293,"recorded_at":1780531400000581,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"b4a16fe6-9763-440b-bf19-bfec570b01d7"},"task_id":"b4a16fe6-9763-440b-bf19-bfec570b01d7","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"b4a16fe6-9763-440b-bf19-bfec570b01d7"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c597","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07a5e-8204-7c61-b778-7e703c0d991a"},"sequence":294,"recorded_at":1780531400000583,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6"},"call_id":"call_01a07a5f301e7c82a78efc14483253d2","text":"Read text file `internal/invcore/invcore.go`.\n1|// Package invcore is the shared test-support core for production-derived\n2|// inventories: production-file selection, fail-closed parsing, and the\n3|// both-direction check harness.\n4|//\n5|// Every package inventory in this repository derives its denominator from\n6|// production source instead of listing it, in three historical\n7|// architectures for the same idea: terminalbackend resolves declared rows\n8|// textually and refuses constructor aliasing outright; provhost executes\n9|// every witness through the production entry point and keys on identifier\n10|// names behind a separate call-site audit; provider instruments constructor\n11|// vars at runtime in TestMain and audits the exercised file:line set\n12|// against AST-derived sites. The weaker bound was the real bound, so this\n13|// core carries the UNION of those directions, not the intersection:\n14|//\n15|//   - ScanProduction owns production-file selection: directory-derived,\n16|//     every *.go except *_test.go, sorted, so a new production file is\n17|//     scanned without anyone remembering it. Zero files is a failure,\n18|//     never a vacuous pass.\n19|//   - MustParse owns fail-closed parsing: an unparseable file fails, never\n20|//     skips. A file the derivation cannot read proves nothing.\n21|//   - DiffSets owns the both-direction harness: derived-without-row\n22|//     (unregistered site) AND row-without-site (orphan row) fail together.\n23|//     The forward direction alone passes vacuously on a truncated\n24|//     derivation.\n25|//   - AuditConstructorReferences owns the alias-bypass union: constructor\n26|//     references outside direct-call position fail outright\n27|//     (terminalbackend direction), import aliases and dot imports resolve\n28|//     against the imported path instead of the local spelling (the shape\n29|//     that walked through every identifier-keyed gate in this repository),\n30|//     and var bindings are references, not calls (provider direction made\n31|//     static). Anything the audit cannot classify — a dot import of a\n32|//     watched path, an unresolved shadowing — fails closed as\n33|//     unclassifiable, never pruned.\n34|//   - SiteRecorder owns the runtime direction (provider/provhost shape):\n35|//     instrumented constructor vars record the production file:line behind\n36|//     every exercised refusal, and the audit requires the exercised set to\n37|//     equal the derived site set in both directions.\n38|//\n39|// All checks come in two spellings: a pure func returning failures for\n40|// negative tests and control plants, and a Must wrapper that fails the\n41|// suite. A gate that can only fatal cannot be planted against, and a plant\n42|// that cannot run proves nothing.\n43|package invcore\n44|\n45|import (\n46|\t\"go/ast\"\n47|\t\"go/parser\"\n48|\t\"go/token\"\n49|\t\"os\"\n50|\t\"path/filepath\"\n51|\t\"sort\"\n52|\t\"strconv\"\n53|\t\"strings\"\n54|)\n55|\n56|// ProductionFile is one parsed production source: basename, full path,\n57|// raw bytes, and syntax parsed with a directory-shared FileSet.\n58|type ProductionFile struct {\n59|\tName   string\n60|\tPath   string\n61|\tSource []byte\n62|\tSyntax *ast.File\n63|\tFile   *token.File\n64|}\n65|\n66|// ScanProduction reads every production file of the directory at dir:\n67|// every *.go except *_test.go, in sorted order. It returns the parsed\n68|// files with their shared FileSet, plus a failure string for every\n69|// fail-closed condition: an unreadable directory, an unreadable file, an\n70|// unparseable file, or zero production files. An empty failure slice with\n71|// an empty file list is impossible by construction.\n72|func ScanProduction(dir string) ([]ProductionFile, *token.FileSet, []string) {\n73|\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(dir)\n74|\tif err != nil {\n75|\t\treturn nil, nil, []string{\"scan production files: read \" + dir + \": \" + err.Error()}\n76|\t}\n77|\tvar names []string\n78|\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n79|\t\tname := entry.Name()\n80|\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n81|\t\t\tcontinue\n82|\t\t}\n83|\t\tnames = append(names, name)\n84|\t}\n85|\tsort.Strings(names)\n86|\tif len(names) == 0 {\n87|\t\treturn nil, nil, []string{\"scanned zero production files in \" + dir + \"; the scanner is broken, not the package\"}\n88|\t}\n89|\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n90|\tvar files []ProductionFile\n91|\tvar failures []string\n92|\tfor _, name := range names {\n93|\t\tpath := filepath.Join(dir, name)\n94|\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n95|\t\tif err != nil {\n96|\t\t\tfailures = append(failures, \"scan production files: read \"+path+\": \"+err.Error())\n97|\t\t\tcontinue\n98|\t\t}\n99|\t\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, path, source, parser.ParseComments)\n100|\t\tif err != nil {\n101|\t\t\tfailures = append(failures, \"scan production files: parse \"+path+\": \"+err.Error()+\"; an unparseable derivation proves nothing\")\n102|\t\t\tcontinue\n103|\t\t}\n104|\t\tfiles = append(files, ProductionFile{\n105|\t\t\tName:   name,\n106|\t\t\tPath:   path,\n107|\t\t\tSource: source,\n108|\t\t\tSyntax: syntax,\n109|\t\t\tFile:   fileSet.File(syntax.Pos()),\n110|\t\t})\n111|\t}\n112|\tif len(files) == 0 && len(failures) == 0 {\n113|\t\tfailures = append(failures, \"derived zero parsed production files in \"+dir+\"; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n114|\t}\n115|\treturn files, fileSet, failures\n116|}\n117|\n118|// ParseSource parses one synthetic source (control plants, classifier\n119|// unit probes) with fail-closed semantics: the failure string is empty on\n120|// success and names the cause otherwise.\n121|func ParseSource(filename string, source []byte) (*ast.File, *token.FileSet, string) {\n122|\treturn ParseBytes(filename, source, parser.ParseComments)\n123|}\n124|\n125|// ParseBytes parses one source with the given parser mode and fail-closed\n126|// semantics: the failure string is empty on success and names the cause\n127|// otherwise. Inventories with a non-standard traversal (recursive walk,\n128|// content prefilter, imports-only scan) keep their traversal and route\n129|// parsing here, so an unparseable file fails identically everywhere.\n130|func ParseBytes(filename string, source []byte, mode parser.Mode) (*ast.File, *token.FileSet, string) {\n131|\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n132|\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, filename, source, mode)\n133|\tif err != nil {\n134|\t\treturn nil, nil, \"parse \" + filename + \": \" + err.Error() + \"; an unparseable derivation proves nothing\"\n135|\t}\n136|\treturn syntax, fileSet, \"\"\n137|}\n138|\n139|// DiffSets is the both-direction harness over string keys: every derived\n140|// key without a row is unregistered, every row without a derived key is\n141|// orphaned. Both lists are sorted. Empty derived input is itself a\n142|// failure: a domain that silently derives nothing is not a measurement,\n143|// and the forward check would otherwise pass vacuously.\n144|func DiffSets(derived, rows map[string]struct{}) (unregistered, orphaned, failures []string) {\n145|\tif len(derived) == 0 {\n146|\t\tfailures = append(failures, \"derived zero sites; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n147|\t}\n148|\tfor key := range derived {\n149|\t\tif _, ok := rows[key]; !ok {\n150|\t\t\tunregistered = append(unregistered, key)\n151|\t\t}\n152|\t}\n153|\tfor key := range rows {\n154|\t\tif _, ok := derived[key]; !ok {\n155|\t\t\torphaned = append(orphaned, key)\n156|\t\t}\n157|\t}\n158|\tsort.Strings(unregistered)\n159|\tsort.Strings(orphaned)\n160|\treturn unregistered, orphaned, failures\n161|}\n162|\n163|// ConstructorSpec declares the refusal constructors one audit watches:\n164|// package-local bare identifiers (mismatchf) and qualified constructors\n165|// matched by IMPORT PATH and member name (errors.New), so an import alias\n166|// cannot change what the audit sees.\n167|type ConstructorSpec struct {\n168|\t// Local names package-local constructor identifiers.\n169|\tLocal map[string]bool\n170|\t// Qualified maps an import path to its watched member names:\n171|\t// {\"errors\": {\"New\": true}, \"fmt\": {\"Errorf\": true}}. A member name\n172|\t// with a trailing \"*\" matches by prefix (\"Errorf*\" covers Errorf\n173|\t// and its Errorf-prefixed kin).\n174|\tQualified map[string]map[string]bool\n175|}\n176|\n177|// qualifiedWatches reports whether member is watched under path,\n178|// honoring trailing-\"*\" prefix entries.\n179|func qualifiedWatches(spec ConstructorSpec, path, member string) bool {\n180|\tmembers, ok := spec.Qualified[path]\n181|\tif !ok {\n182|\t\treturn false\n183|\t}\n184|\tif members[member] {\n185|\t\treturn true\n186|\t}\n187|\tfor watched := range members {\n188|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(watched, \"*\") && strings.HasPrefix(member, strings.TrimSuffix(watched, \"*\")) {\n189|\t\t\treturn true\n190|\t\t}\n191|\t}\n192|\treturn false\n193|}\n194|\n195|// AuditConstructorReferences fails every constructor reference outside\n196|// direct-call position: aliases, var bindings, arguments, struct fields,\n197|// and shadows. Import aliases resolve through the file's import specs, so\n198|// `import errs \"errors\"; errs.New(\"…\")` attributes to errors.New and\n199|// `alias := errs.New` fails like any other binding. A dot import of a\n200|// watched path or any other shape the audit cannot classify fails closed\n201|// as unclassifiable instead of passing silently. Direct calls and the\n202|// constructors' own declarations are the only allowed positions.\n203|func AuditConstructorReferences(syntax *ast.File, fileSet *token.FileSet, display string, spec ConstructorSpec) []string {\n204|\timports := resolveImports(syntax, spec)\n205|\tfor path := range spec.Qualified {\n206|\t\tif dot, ok := imports.dot[path]; ok && dot {\n207|\t\t\treturn []string{display + \": dot-imports watched path \" + strconv.Quote(path) + \"; the audit cannot attribute bare \" + constructorMembers(spec.Qualified[path]) + \", qualify the import or widen the audit\"}\n208|\t\t}\n209|\t}\n210|\tallowed := map[token.Pos]bool{}\n211|\tast.Inspect(syntax, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n212|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n213|\t\tif ok && spec.Local[declaration.Name.Name] {\n214|\t\t\t// The declaration name itself is allowed, but the body\n215|\t\t\t// still scans: a direct call nested inside the funnel\n216|\t\t\t// body is attributable and must stay allowed.\n217|\t\t\tallowed[declaration.Name.Pos()] = true\n218|\t\t\treturn true\n219|\t\t}\n220|\t\tcall, ok := node.(*ast.CallExpr)\n221|\t\tif !ok {\n222|\t\t\treturn true\n223|\t\t}\n224|\t\tif ident, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident); ok && spec.Local[ident.Name] {\n225|\t\t\tallowed[ident.Pos()] = true\n226|\t\t\treturn true\n227|\t\t}\n228|\t\tif selector, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.SelectorExpr); ok {\n229|\t\t\tif receiver, ok := selector.X.(*ast.Ident); ok {\n230|\t\t\t\tif qualifiedWatches(spec, imports.pathOf(receiver.Name), selector.Sel.Name) {\n231|\t\t\t\t\tallowed[selector.Sel.Pos()] = true\n232|\t\t\t\t}\n233|\t\t\t}\n234|\t\t}\n235|\t\treturn true\n236|\t})\n237|\tvar failures []string\n238|\tast.Inspect(syntax, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n239|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n240|\t\tif ok && spec.Local[declaration.Name.Name] {\n241|\t\t\t// Descend: the declaration name is allowlisted by\n242|\t\t\t// position, but references nested in the funnel body\n243|\t\t\t// still audit.\n244|\t\t\treturn true\n245|\t\t}\n246|\t\tident, ok := node.(*ast.Ident)\n247|\t\tif !ok || allowed[ident.Pos()] {\n248|\t\t\treturn true\n249|\t\t}\n250|\t\tif spec.Local[ident.Name] {\n251|\t\t\tif _, declared := imports.names[ident.Name]; declared {\n252|\t\t\t\tfailures = append(failures, display+\":\"+positionOf(fileSet, ident.Pos())+\": constructor \"+strconv.Quote(ident.Name)+\" shadowed by an import or declaration the audit cannot classify; rename it or widen the audit\")\n253|\t\t\t\treturn true\n254|\t\t\t}\n255|\t\t\tfailures = append(failures, display+\":\"+positionOf(fileSet, ident.Pos())+\": constructor \"+strconv.Quote(ident.Name)+\" referenced outside direct-call position; an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, call it directly\")\n256|\t\t\treturn true\n257|\t\t}\n258|\t\treturn true\n259|\t})\n260|\tast.Inspect(syntax, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n261|\t\tselector, ok := node.(*ast.SelectorExpr)\n262|\t\tif !ok || allowed[selector.Sel.Pos()] {\n263|\t\t\treturn true\n264|\t\t}\n265|\t\treceiver, ok := selector.X.(*ast.Ident)\n266|\t\tif !ok {\n267|\t\t\treturn true\n268|\t\t}\n269|\t\tif qualifiedWatches(spec, imports.pathOf(receiver.Name), selector.Sel.Name) {\n270|\t\t\tfailures = append(failures, display+\":\"+positionOf(fileSet, selector.Sel.Pos())+\": constructor \"+strconv.Quote(receiver.Name+\".\"+selector.Sel.Name)+\" referenced outside direct-call position; an aliased construction cannot be inventoried, call it directly\")\n271|\t\t}\n272|\t\treturn true\n273|\t})\n274|\tsort.Strings(failures)\n275|\treturn failures\n276|}\n277|\n278|// FunPosition reports the audited position of a call's function: the\n279|// identifier for bare calls, the selector member for qualified calls.\n280|// WatchedCallPositions keys on exactly these positions.\n281|func FunPosition(call *ast.CallExpr) (token.Pos, bool) {\n282|\tswitch fun := call.Fun.(type) {\n283|\tcase *ast.Ident:\n284|\t\treturn fun.Pos(), true\n285|\tcase *ast.SelectorExpr:\n286|\t\treturn fun.Sel.Pos(), true\n287|\tdefault:\n288|\t\treturn token.NoPos, false\n289|\t}\n290|}\n291|\n292|// WatchedCallPositions returns the audited positions of every direct\n293|// call to a watched constructor in syntax: the attribution set. Callers\n294|// use it to attribute each watched construction to its enclosing\n295|// function (an allowlist scan), while AuditConstructorReferences owns\n296|// the alias direction over the same spec.\n297|func WatchedCallPositions(syntax *ast.File, spec ConstructorSpec) map[token.Pos]bool {\n298|\timports := resolveImports(syntax, spec)\n299|\tpositions := map[token.Pos]bool{}\n300|\tast.Inspect(syntax, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c599","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07a5e-8204-7c61-b778-7e703c0d991a"},"sequence":295,"recorded_at":1780531400000585,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6"},"call_id":"call_01a07a5f30d17d41be848d4b2ea64bfb","text":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_site_audit_test.go`.\n1|// Exercised-site audit for the terminal backend refusal arms.\n2|//\n3|// The failure this file exists to prevent: a declared, witnessed arm going\n4|// dead by construction while the whole suite stays green. Witnesses assert\n5|// the (code, detail) pair at a public entry; several arms share one pair\n6|// (62 of 184 witnessed arms share their clause with a sibling), so a\n7|// widened earlier guard swallows a later arm's inputs and the later\n8|// witness still passes through the sibling. That plant (P8:\n9|// CheckEntrypoint's first session parse widened to also compare, killing\n10|// the second parse and the comparison arms) left the derived set\n11|// byte-identical, the bijection at 210/210, and every witness green.\n12|//\n13|// The audit closes it the way provider and provhost already do: every\n14|// production refusal construction records its file:line at runtime\n15|// (through refuse/mismatchf/integrityFailure, armed by TestMain below),\n16|// and the post-run audit requires every derived non-bound line to have\n17|// fired at least once, and every fired line to be derived. A shadowed arm\n18|// never fires, so it reddens here as a derived site without an exercised\n19|// path. Bound arms (26 rows no input can reach) are exempt by their\n20|// declared rows, mapped to lines by TestDerivedSiteLinesAreExactlyRowed,\n21|// never by hand.\n22|//\n23|// Recording is off (nil hook) in production: construction is then a pure\n24|// allocation with zero behavior change.\n25|package terminalbackend\n26|\n27|import (\n28|\t\"flag\"\n29|\t\"fmt\"\n30|\t\"os\"\n31|\t\"runtime\"\n32|\t\"sort\"\n33|\t\"strconv\"\n34|\t\"strings\"\n35|\t\"sync\"\n36|\t\"testing\"\n37|\n38|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/invcore\"\n39|)\n40|\n41|// refusalSiteRecorder is the shared core's runtime direction: the\n42|// production file:line behind every refusal construction during the test\n43|// run, plus the wire codes those refusals carried. The hook is armed in\n44|// TestMain, so an aliased constructor still executes the funnel and\n45|// records its real production site: the runtime direction of the\n46|// alias-bypass union.\n47|var refusalSiteRecorder = invcore.NewSiteRecorder()\n48|\n49|func TestMain(main *testing.M) {\n50|\trecordRefusal = func(code, detail string) {\n51|\t\t// Skip counts the frames between Record and the production\n52|\t\t// site: the hook closure plus the funnel frame, matching the\n53|\t\t// provider/provhost swapped-constructor convention exactly\n54|\t\t// (pinned by TestRefusalSiteAttributionIsExact, not by reading).\n55|\t\trefusalSiteRecorder.Record(code, 2)\n56|\t}\n57|\tcode := main.Run()\n58|\tif code == 0 && fullPackageTestRun() {\n59|\t\tif failures := auditRefusalInventory(); len(failures) != 0 {\n60|\t\t\tfor _, failure := range failures {\n61|\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, failure)\n62|\t\t\t}\n63|\t\t\tcode = 1\n64|\t\t}\n65|\t}\n66|\tos.Exit(code)\n67|}\n68|\n69|func fullPackageTestRun() bool {\n70|\tselected := flag.Lookup(\"test.run\")\n71|\treturn selected == nil || selected.Value.String() == \"\"\n72|}\n73|\n74|// refusalAuditDomain is the captured in-band derivation the post-run\n75|// audit compares the exercised set against. It is captured by\n76|// TestDerivedSiteLinesAreExactlyRowed (which runs with a *testing.T and\n77|// can use the rich derivation) because TestMain has no *testing.T to\n78|// derive with. The audit fails closed when the domain is missing: a\n79|// scoped (-run) run never reaches the audit by fullPackageTestRun.\n80|type refusalAuditDomain struct {\n81|\tderived   map[string]struct{}\n82|\tbound     map[string]struct{}\n83|\twantCodes []string\n84|}\n85|\n86|var auditDomainMu sync.Mutex\n87|var capturedAuditDomain *refusalAuditDomain\n88|\n89|// TestDerivedSiteLinesAreExactlyRowed is the static half of site\n90|// attribution: every derived arm line resolves to exactly one declared\n91|// row and every declared row to exactly one derived line, and it captures\n92|// the domain the post-run exercised-site audit compares against. Bound\n93|// rows resolve to lines too: the exemption is row-derived, never listed.\n94|func TestDerivedSiteLinesAreExactlyRowed(t *testing.T) {\n95|\tt.Parallel()\n96|\n97|\tarms := deriveRefusalArms(t)\n98|\trows := declaredRows()\n99|\trowByKey := make(map[string]declaredRefusalArm, len(rows))\n100|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n101|\t\tkey := describeRow(row)\n102|\t\tif _, duplicate := rowByKey[key]; duplicate {\n103|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"declared row %s occurs twice; the mapping cannot attribute it\", key)\n104|\t\t}\n105|\t\trowByKey[key] = row\n106|\t}\n107|\tlineToRow := make(map[string]string)\n108|\trowToLine := make(map[string]string)\n109|\tfor _, arm := range arms {\n110|\t\t// The arm key space is occurrence-aware but line-free, and the\n111|\t\t// row key space is identical, so describeArm maps lines onto\n112|\t\t// rows through the shared identity without ever listing a line\n113|\t\t// by hand. (Line is not part of the key: describeArm never\n114|\t\t// reads it.)\n115|\t\tsite := arm.file + \":\" + strconv.Itoa(arm.line)\n116|\t\tkey := describeArm(arm)\n117|\t\trow, known := rowByKey[key]\n118|\t\tif !known {\n119|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"derived arm %s at %s resolves to no declared row\", key, site)\n120|\t\t\tcontinue\n121|\t\t}\n122|\t\trowKey := describeRow(row)\n123|\t\tif first, duplicate := lineToRow[site]; duplicate {\n124|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"derived line %s attributes rows %s and %s\", site, first, rowKey)\n125|\t\t\tcontinue\n126|\t\t}\n127|\t\tlineToRow[site] = rowKey\n128|\t\tif first, duplicate := rowToLine[rowKey]; duplicate {\n129|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"declared row %s resolves to lines %s and %s\", rowKey, first, site)\n130|\t\t\tcontinue\n131|\t\t}\n132|\t\trowToLine[rowKey] = site\n133|\t}\n134|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n135|\t\tif _, ok := rowToLine[describeRow(row)]; !ok {\n136|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"declared row %s resolves to no derived line\", describeRow(row))\n137|\t\t}\n138|\t}\n139|\tderived := make(map[string]struct{}, len(lineToRow))\n140|\tfor site := range lineToRow {\n141|\t\tderived[site] = struct{}{}\n142|\t}\n143|\tbound := make(map[string]struct{})\n144|\tfor site, rowKey := range lineToRow {\n145|\t\tif rowByKey[rowKey].bound != \"\" {\n146|\t\t\tbound[site] = struct{}{}\n147|\t\t}\n148|\t}\n149|\tsymbols := productionCodeSymbols(t)\n150|\tvar wantCodes []string\n151|\tfor symbol, wire := range symbols {\n152|\t\tif armlessCodes[symbol] {\n153|\t\t\tcontinue\n154|\t\t}\n155|\t\twantCodes = append(wantCodes, wire)\n156|\t}\n157|\tsort.Strings(wantCodes)\n158|\tauditDomainMu.Lock()\n159|\tcapturedAuditDomain = &refusalAuditDomain{derived: derived, bound: bound, wantCodes: wantCodes}\n160|\tauditDomainMu.Unlock()\n161|\tt.Logf(\"refusal-site audit domain: %d derived lines, %d bound-exempt, %d wire codes\",\n162|\t\tlen(derived), len(bound), len(wantCodes))\n163|}\n164|\n165|// auditRefusalInventory derives nothing: it compares the exercised\n166|// file:line set against the captured domain in both directions, plus the\n167|// closed wire-code set. A shadowed-dead arm never fires, so it fails here\n168|// as a derived site without an exercised path even though its pair still\n169|// refuses through its sibling and every witness stays green.\n170|func auditRefusalInventory() []string {\n171|\tauditDomainMu.Lock()\n172|\tdomain := capturedAuditDomain\n173|\tauditDomainMu.Unlock()\n174|\tif domain == nil || len(domain.derived) == 0 {\n175|\t\treturn []string{\"refusal-site audit: no captured audit domain; the mapping test did not run (full suite required)\"}\n176|\t}\n177|\tvar failures []string\n178|\texercised := refusalSiteRecorder.Sites()\n179|\tvar outside []string\n180|\tfor site := range exercised {\n181|\t\tif _, ok := domain.derived[site]; !ok {\n182|\t\t\toutside = append(outside, site)\n183|\t\t}\n184|\t}\n185|\tsort.Strings(outside)\n186|\tif len(outside) != 0 {\n187|\t\tfailures = append(failures, \"refusal-site audit: exercised refusal sites outside the derived inventory; the derivation is short: \"+strings.Join(outside, \", \"))\n188|\t}\n189|\tvar missing []string\n190|\tfor site := range domain.derived {\n191|\t\tif _, ok := domain.bound[site]; ok {\n192|\t\t\tcontinue\n193|\t\t}\n194|\t\tif _, ok := exercised[site]; !ok {\n195|\t\t\tmissing = append(missing, site)\n196|\t\t}\n197|\t}\n198|\tsort.Strings(missing)\n199|\tif len(missing) != 0 {\n200|\t\tfailures = append(failures, \"refusal-site audit: derived refusal sites without an exercised path (shadowed dead or unwitnessed): \"+strings.Join(missing, \", \"))\n201|\t}\n202|\tcodes := refusalSiteRecorder.Codes()\n203|\tif fmt.Sprintf(\"%v\", codes) != fmt.Sprintf(\"%v\", domain.wantCodes) {\n204|\t\tfailures = append(failures, fmt.Sprintf(\"refusal-site audit: observed refusal codes = %v, want closed set %v\", codes, domain.wantCodes))\n205|\t}\n206|\treturn failures\n207|}\n208|\n209|// TestRefusalSiteAttributionIsExact pins the recorder skip empirically:\n210|// a refusal built on the marked line must attribute to this file at that\n211|// line through each funnel.\n212|//\n213|// SEQUENTIAL BY DESIGN (no t.Parallel): it swaps the package hook, which\n214|// races with every parallel witness recording into the global recorder.\n215|// Sequential tests run exclusively before the parallel phase resumes, so\n216|// the swap is exclusive. Do not parallelize this test.\n217|func TestRefusalSiteAttributionIsExact(t *testing.T) {\n218|\tprobe := invcore.NewSiteRecorder()\n219|\tprevious := recordRefusal\n220|\trecordRefusal = func(code, detail string) {\n221|\t\tprobe.Record(code, 2)\n222|\t}\n223|\tdefer func() { recordRefusal = previous }()\n224|\n225|\t_, _, refuseLine, _ := runtime.Caller(0)\n226|\trefused := refuse(&Error{Code: CodeNotFound, Detail: \"attribution probe\"}) // want refuseLine+1\n227|\tif refused.Code != CodeNotFound || refused.Detail != \"attribution probe\" {\n228|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"refuse() = %+v, want the wrapped literal unchanged: recording never alters the refusal\", refused)\n229|\t}\n230|\t_, _, mismatchLine, _ := runtime.Caller(0)\n231|\tmismatched := mismatchf(\"attribution probe\") // want mismatchLine+1\n232|\tif mismatched.Code != CodeMismatch || mismatched.Detail != \"attribution probe\" {\n233|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"mismatchf() = %+v, want CodeMismatch at the static detail\", mismatched)\n234|\t}\n235|\t_, _, integrityLine, _ := runtime.Caller(0)\n236|\tintegrity := integrityFailure(\"attribution probe\") // want integrityLine+1\n237|\tif integrity.Code != CodeIntegrityFailure || integrity.Detail != \"attribution probe\" {\n238|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"integrityFailure() = %+v, want CodeIntegrityFailure at the static detail\", integrity)\n239|\t}\n240|\tsites := probe.Sites()\n241|\tfor _, want := range []string{\n242|\t\t\"refusal_site_audit_test.go:\" + strconv.Itoa(refuseLine+1),\n243|\t\t\"refusal_site_audit_test.go:\" + strconv.Itoa(mismatchLine+1),\n244|\t\t\"refusal_site_audit_test.go:\" + strconv.Itoa(integrityLine+1),\n245|\t} {\n246|\t\tif _, ok := sites[want]; !ok {\n247|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"attributed sites = %v, want %s recorded: the skip is wrong and the audit is blind\", sites, want)\n248|\t\t}\n249|\t}\n250|\tif len(sites) != 3 {\n251|\t\tt.Errorf(\"attributed sites = %v, want exactly the three probe sites\", sites)\n252|\t}\n253|}\n254|\n255|// TestRefuseFunnelRejectsAliases is the committed tb-level proof of the\n256|// alias-bypass union for the new funnel: a direct refuse call is\n257|// admitted, a var-bound refuse, a var-bound mismatchf (the P1 shape), and\n258|// an import-aliased errors.New (the P2 shape) all fail. Dropping refuse\n259|// from the watch list (N-tb-refuse) kills this test while the downstream\n260|// behav mask stays green.\n261|func TestRefuseFunnelRejectsAliases(t *testing.T) {\n262|\tt.Parallel()\n263|\n264|\tadmitted := `package terminalbackend\n265|func direct() *Error { return refuse(&Error{Code: CodeNotFound, Detail: \"x\"}) }\n266|`\n267|\tsyntax, fileSet, failure := invcore.ParseSource(\"direct.go\", []byte(admitted))\n268|\tif failure != \"\" {\n269|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse admitted source: %s\", failure)\n270|\t}\n271|\tif failures := invcore.AuditConstructorReferences(syntax, fileSet, \"direct.go\", refusalConstructorSpec()); len(failures) != 0 {\n272|\t\tt.Errorf(\"direct refuse call rejected: %v\", failures)\n273|\t}\n274|\trejected := map[string]string{\n275|\t\t\"var-bound refuse\": \"package terminalbackend\\nvar aliasedRefuse = refuse\\n\" +\n276|\t\t\t\"func indirect() *Error { return aliasedRefuse(&Error{Code: CodeNotFound, Detail: \\\"x\\\"}) }\\n\",\n277|\t\t\"var-bound mismatchf (P1)\": \"package terminalbackend\\nvar aliasedMismatch = mismatchf\\n\" +\n278|\t\t\t\"func indirect() *Error { return aliasedMismatch(\\\"x\\\") }\\n\",\n279|\t\t\"import-aliased errors.New (P2)\": \"package terminalbackend\\nimport errs \\\"errors\\\"\\n\" +\n280|\t\t\t\"var mintPlain = errs.New\\nfunc indirect() error { return mintPlain(\\\"x\\\") }\\n\",\n281|\t}\n282|\tfor name, source := range rejected {\n283|\t\tsyntax, fileSet, failure := invcore.ParseSource(\"plant.go\", []byte(source))\n284|\t\tif failure != \"\" {\n285|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s plant: %s\", name, failure)\n286|\t\t}\n287|\t\tfailures := invcore.AuditConstructorReferences(syntax, fileSet, \"plant.go\", refusalConstructorSpec())\n288|\t\tif len(failures) == 0 {\n289|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%s admitted: the alias bypasses attribution\", name)\n290|\t\t}\n291|\t}\n292|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
