{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c75f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07a5e-8204-7c61-b778-7e703c0d991a"},"sequence":522,"recorded_at":1780531400001039,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6"},"call_id":"call_01a07a5fbdd67e52904922a9f54e1997","text":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/digit_guard_census_test.go`.\n1|// Derived digit-guard census over the provider-protocol leaf.\n2|//\n3|// The failure this file exists to prevent: a digit-parsing gate added,\n4|// narrowed, or widened anywhere in this leaf while the suite stays\n5|// green. It happened four rounds in a row — a saturation guard\n6|// witnessed far from its own edge, an exponent bound witnessed 44\n7|// bytes above its true edge, an uncensused semverMajor, and finally a\n8|// pre-multiply guard (`value > 100` in descriptorGeometry) whose\n9|// narrowing to its own arithmetic edge (`value > 922337203685477580`)\n10|// admitted a 37-digit literal as 1 while every shipped vector still\n11|// refused. Each round closed one site with one hand-written row while\n12|// the census listed its own sites, so the next site was invisible by\n13|// construction.\n14|//\n15|// This census derives its denominator from production instead of\n16|// listing it: it parses every production file of internal/\n17|// terminalbackend and internal/provhost (directory-derived, so a new\n18|// file is scanned without anyone remembering it) and enumerates both\n19|// digit-guard shapes in one pass:\n20|//\n21|//   - char: an ordering comparison against a decimal digit rune\n22|//     (`c < '0' || c > '9'` and its spellings, refuse-form or\n23|//     accept-form, including the digit case of a hex decoder);\n24|//   - bound: an ordering comparison against a decimal accumulator —\n25|//     an identifier the same function accumulates through `* 10`\n26|//     (`value > N` / `major > N`, before or after the multiply).\n27|//\n28|// Every derived site carries exactly one declared row: a char row\n29|// names its reachable rejected class, a bound row names its\n30|// arithmetic-edge threshold and its witness. The census fails closed\n31|// in three directions: a derived site with no row, a row with no\n32|// derived site, and a site the classifier cannot place (an equality\n33|// against a digit rune, a chain mixing digit and accumulator\n34|// comparisons, a chain mixing either with unrelated comparisons, or\n35|// a comparison with accumulators on both sides). A zero-file scan, a\n36|// zero-site derivation, an unparseable file, a row with an empty\n37|// claim, and a row naming a test that does not exist are fatal too.\n38|//\n39|// The derivation keys on structure, never on identifier names: rune\n40|// literals and `* 10` accumulations survive renaming, var bindings,\n41|// and import aliases. Control plants prove it (see the battery\n42|// record): a fourth digit gate through a var binding and one through\n43|// an import-aliased file both fail as unregistered sites.\n44|//\n45|// Stated bounds (not inferred):\n46|//   - Non-digit rune guards (`== '.'`, `!= '\\\\'`, `!= 'u'`, the\n47|//     `0xed`/`0xa0` byte ranges) are a different class and invisible\n48|//     to this enumerator. A digit-rune novelty (`== '0'`, `!= '9'`)\n49|//     is derived and fails as unclassifiable.\n50|//   - Digit spellings outside the comparison classifier, completed per\n51|//     review N-R1 (three semantically identical spellings; the earlier\n52|//     \"no such site in either package\" claim was false for the third\n53|//     and is corrected here, not repeated):\n54|//     1. integer code points (`c < 0x30`, `c > 57`) are ENUMERATED:\n55|//     digitGuardDigitRune admits token.INT 48..57 in every base,\n56|//     pinned by TestDigitGuardDigitRuneAdmitsCodePointSpellings;\n57|//     2. named rune constants (`const zero = '0'; c < zero`) are\n58|//     OUTSIDE: an identifier is not a literal, so the comparison\n59|//     classifies as other. A pure named-constant chain (every leaf\n60|//     other) prunes silently — a control plant of an additive pure\n61|//     named-const digit gate in provhost/protocol.go leaves both\n62|//     packages green, so this spelling is a genuine blind spot, not\n63|//     a fail-closed one. Only a mixed chain (a named-constant leaf\n64|//     beside a literal-digit or accumulator leaf) fails as\n65|//     unclassifiable. No such site exists in either package today\n66|//     (reviewer-grepped at N-R1, re-verified for this leaf by AST\n67|//     scan: zero digit-valued named constants and zero such\n68|//     comparisons); the absence is a stated bound, not a derived\n69|//     pin.\n70|//     3. strconv-delegated admission is OUTSIDE the comparison\n71|//     classifier: it is not a comparison at all, so there is no\n72|//     chain to classify. One such site EXISTS:\n73|//     internal/provhost/opdecode.go rawUint53\n74|//     (`strconv.ParseUint(literal, 10, 64)` + error branch +\n75|//     magnitude bound `parsed > maxUint53`). It is behaviorally\n76|//     pinned, not censused: narrowing the bound to `maxUint53+1`\n77|//     (admitting exactly 2^53) reddens\n78|//     TestDecodeQuiesceRefusals/count_overflow, which refuses 2^53\n79|//     as \"not a uint53\" (battery row B-provhost-strconv-bound\n80|//     reproduces exactly that plant and kill). A second delegated\n81|//     site is covered only if it carries the same shape of\n82|//     behavioral pin; the census still fails closed on every\n83|//     comparison it CAN see.\n84|//   - The hex letter cases (`>= 'a'`, `<= 'F'`) carry no digit rune\n85|//     and are invisible; only the digit case of each hex decoder is\n86|//     rowed. The decoder's exactness across all three cases rests\n87|//     with the canonical-JSON agreement sweeps the hex rows name.\n88|//   - An accumulator with no guard has no bound to row: a missing\n89|//     guard is caught by the overflow-vector tests, not here.\n90|//   - Shadowing an accumulator name inside its own function would\n91|//     misattribute the comparison; no such shadowing exists today.\n92|package terminalbackend_test\n93|\n94|import (\n95|\t\"bytes\"\n96|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/invcore\"\n97|\t\"go/ast\"\n98|\t\"go/printer\"\n99|\t\"go/token\"\n100|\t\"os\"\n101|\t\"path/filepath\"\n102|\t\"sort\"\n103|\t\"strconv\"\n104|\t\"strings\"\n105|\t\"testing\"\n106|\n107|\tterminalbackend \"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n108|)\n109|\n110|// digitGuardSite is one derived production guard: a maximal ||/&&\n111|// chain of comparisons (or one lone comparison) mentioning a digit\n112|// rune or a decimal accumulator, keyed by package directory, file,\n113|// enclosing function, shape, and printer-normalized expression. Two\n114|// identical guards in one function share a key and fail the census\n115|// until they are disambiguated: hiding behind a sibling row is a\n116|// silent admit.\n117|type digitGuardSite struct {\n118|\tdir      string\n119|\tfunction string\n120|\tfile     string\n121|\tkind     string\n122|\texpr     string\n123|}\n124|\n125|// digitGuardRow is the declared counterpart of one site. A char row\n126|// states the reachable rejected class; a bound row states the\n127|// arithmetic-edge threshold and the witness literal that pins it.\n128|// Tests names the driving tests, which must exist.\n129|type digitGuardRow struct {\n130|\tdir       string\n131|\tfile      string\n132|\tfunction  string\n133|\tkind      string\n134|\texpr      string\n135|\trejected  string\n136|\tthreshold string\n137|\twitness   string\n138|\ttests     []string\n139|}\n140|\n141|// digitGuardRows declares every digit guard in the leaf. The expr\n142|// column is the printer-normalized chain text the derivation\n143|// computes; it is exact on purpose, so editing a bound orphans its\n144|// row instead of passing silently.\n145|var digitGuardRows = []digitGuardRow{\n146|\t{\n147|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"descriptor.go\", function: \"descriptorGeometry\",\n148|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `digit < '0' || digit > '9'`,\n149|\t\trejected: \"reachable {-, +, ., e, E}: json.Number literals spell only [0-9.+eE-], so / (0x2F) and : (0x3A) die in the strict decoder before the gate runs (pinned by TestDigitCensusAdjacentsNeverReachGeometryGate); + is equivalent by reachability, legal only after e/E which refuse first\",\n150|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestParseProviderDescriptorValueRefusals\", \"TestDigitCensusAdjacentsNeverReachGeometryGate\"},\n151|\t},\n152|\t{\n153|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"manifest.go\", function: \"readUTF16EscapeUnit\",\n154|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `digit >= '0' && digit <= '9'`,\n155|\t\trejected: \"the digit case of the three-case hex decoder: bytes outside 0-9a-fA-F reach the refuse arm (return false, refused as a document syntax/surrogate escape); the case admits exactly 0-9\",\n156|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestDocumentSurrogateEscapeRefused\", \"TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON\", \"TestDocumentHexEscapeDigitBoundaryRefused\"},\n157|\t},\n158|\t{\n159|\t\tdir: \"provhost\", file: \"protocol.go\", function: \"parseMajor\",\n160|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `digit < '0' || digit > '9'`,\n161|\t\trejected: \"every non-digit byte in the major component (JSON string domain, so any byte is reachable): adjacents / and : witnessed in major position\",\n162|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry\"},\n163|\t},\n164|\t{\n165|\t\tdir: \"provhost\", file: \"protocol.go\", function: \"parseMajor\",\n166|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `rest[i] < '0' || rest[i] > '9'`,\n167|\t\trejected: \"every non-digit byte in each rest component: adjacents / and : witnessed in both minor and patch positions\",\n168|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry\"},\n169|\t},\n170|\t{\n171|\t\tdir: \"provhost\", file: \"surrogate.go\", function: \"readHexUnit\",\n172|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `b >= '0' && b <= '9'`,\n173|\t\trejected: \"the digit branch of the hex if-chain: bytes outside 0-9a-fA-F reach the refuse arm (return false, refused as a lone surrogate escape); the branch admits exactly 0-9\",\n174|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestProductionEntriesRefuseLoneSurrogateEscapes\", \"TestSurrogateGateDerivedSweepAgreesWithCanonicalJSON\", \"TestProductionEntriesRefuseHexDigitBoundaryEscapes\"},\n175|\t},\n176|\t{\n177|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"descriptor.go\", function: \"descriptorGeometry\",\n178|\t\tkind: \"bound\", expr: `value > 100`,\n179|\t\tthreshold: \"100: refuse on the first digit past the bound, before the multiply; value is at most 100 here so value*10+9 cannot wrap on any platform\",\n180|\t\twitness:   \"9223372036854775808000000000000000001 (37 digits): admitted as 1 when the guard narrows to floor(MaxInt/10) = 922337203685477580, refused by every threshold at or below 92233720368547758\",\n181|\t\ttests:     []string{\"TestParseProviderDescriptorGeometryOverflowVectors\"},\n182|\t},\n183|\t{\n184|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"descriptor.go\", function: \"descriptorGeometry\",\n185|\t\tkind: \"bound\", expr: `value < 1 || value > 1000`,\n186|\t\tthreshold: \"lower 1 / upper 1000: the post-accumulation range deciding the 1..1000 bound after the loop\",\n187|\t\twitness:   \"boundary pair 0/1 and 1000/1001, plus 65535\",\n188|\t\ttests:     []string{\"TestParseProviderDescriptorValueRefusals\", \"TestParseProviderDescriptorGeometryBounds\"},\n189|\t},\n190|\t{\n191|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"semverMajor\",\n192|\t\tkind: \"bound\", expr: `major > (math.MaxInt-digit)/10`,\n193|\t\tthreshold: \"floor((MaxInt-digit)/10): saturate to MaxInt, never wrap; largest admitted 9223372036854775807, MaxInt+1 saturates\",\n194|\t\twitness:   \"922337203685477580801.0.0 with neighbours 800/802: walks the accumulator to MaxInt/10 and aliases native major 1 when the guard narrows to MaxInt/10\",\n195|\t\ttests:     []string{\"TestSemverMajorSaturationEdge\"},\n196|\t},\n197|\t{\n198|\t\tdir: \"provhost\", file: \"protocol.go\", function: \"parseMajor\",\n199|\t\tkind: \"bound\", expr: `major > (math.MaxInt-step)/10`,\n200|\t\tthreshold: \"floor((MaxInt-step)/10): saturate to MaxInt, never wrap; largest admitted 9223372036854775807, MaxInt+1 saturates\",\n201|\t\twitness:   \"922337203685477580802.0.0 with neighbours 801/803: walks the accumulator to MaxInt/10 and aliases native major 2 when the guard narrows to MaxInt/10\",\n202|\t\ttests:     []string{\"TestParseMajorSaturationEdge\", \"TestParseMajorNeverWraps\"},\n203|\t},\n204|}\n205|\n206|// digitGuardKey identifies one site or row in both directions.\n207|func digitGuardKey(dir, file, function, kind, expr string) string {\n208|\treturn dir + \"|\" + file + \"|\" + function + \"|\" + kind + \"|\" + expr\n209|}\n210|\n211|// TestDigitCensusCoversEveryLeafGuard derives every digit guard from\n212|// leaf production source and requires each to resolve to exactly one\n213|// declared row naming a real test, and every declared row to resolve\n214|// to exactly one derived guard.\n215|func TestDigitCensusCoversEveryLeafGuard(t *testing.T) {\n216|\tt.Parallel()\n217|\n218|\tsites, unclassifiable, files := deriveDigitGuardSites(t)\n219|\tif len(unclassifiable) > 0 {\n220|\t\tsort.Strings(unclassifiable)\n221|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unclassifiable digit-guard shapes (%d), classify them before the suite passes:\\n%s\",\n222|\t\t\tlen(unclassifiable), strings.Join(unclassifiable, \"\\n\"))\n223|\t}\n224|\tseen := map[string]int{}\n225|\tfor _, site := range sites {\n226|\t\tseen[digitGuardKey(site.dir, site.file, site.function, site.kind, site.expr)]++\n227|\t}\n228|\tfor key, count := range seen {\n229|\t\tif count > 1 {\n230|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived digit guard %q occurs %d times; disambiguate the rows instead of hiding behind a sibling\", key, count)\n231|\t\t}\n232|\t}\n233|\tbyKey := map[string]digitGuardSite{}\n234|\tfor _, site := range sites {\n235|\t\tbyKey[digitGuardKey(site.dir, site.file, site.function, site.kind, site.expr)] = site\n236|\t}\n237|\ttests := digitCensusTestNames(t)\n238|\tvar unregistered []string\n239|\tfor _, site := range sites {\n240|\t\tkey := digitGuardKey(site.dir, site.file, site.function, site.kind, site.expr)\n241|\t\tfound := false\n242|\t\tfor _, row := range digitGuardRows {\n243|\t\t\tif digitGuardKey(row.dir, row.file, row.function, row.kind, row.expr) == key {\n244|\t\t\t\tfound = true\n245|\t\t\t\tbreak\n246|\t\t\t}\n247|\t\t}\n248|\t\tif !found {\n249|\t\t\tunregistered = append(unregistered, \"unregistered \"+site.kind+\" site \"+key)\n250|\t\t}\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
