{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d015","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07a5e-8204-7c61-b778-7e703c0d991a"},"sequence":1637,"recorded_at":1780531400003269,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"3a777705-0dbb-48de-9235-35f8487111b9"},"task_id":"3a777705-0dbb-48de-9235-35f8487111b9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"3a777705-0dbb-48de-9235-35f8487111b9","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 157-169\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-// The bound and grammar arms omit BackendID on purpose: a value refused\n-// there is arbitrary input the grammar never admitted, and the package\n-// posture is that refusals never echo unvalidated data. Only the\n-// reserved-namespace arm names the identity, because its input already\n-// passed the grammar. That holds package-wide by construction: every\n-// other site that names a BackendID validates it through ParseID or\n-// mustParseID first — Registration.validate and TrustEntry.validate via\n-// mustParseID; Resolve, RequireRestoreBinding, CheckVersionTuple, and\n-// CheckProviderDescriptor via ParseID at the entry; ParseManifest,\n-// ParseProbe, and ParseEvidence via ParseID at document admission, so\n-// the manifest/probe/generation/drift arms consume validated structs;\n-// New and RegisterExternal via constants and already-validated records —\n-// so a named BackendID is always a validated identity, never raw input.\n+// The bound and grammar arms omit BackendID on purpose: a value refused\n+// there is arbitrary input the grammar never admitted, and the package\n+// posture is that refusals never echo unvalidated data. Only the\n+// reserved-namespace arm names the identity, because its input already\n+// passed the grammar.\n+//\n+// Every other site that names a BackendID is covered by the entry census\n+// in backend_id_entry_census_test.go, keyed by (site, reaching exported\n+// entry): Registration.validate and TrustEntry.validate via mustParseID;\n+// Resolve, RequireRestoreBinding, CheckVersionTuple,\n+// CheckProviderDescriptor and Reconcile via ParseID at the entry;\n+// ParseManifest, ParseProbe and ParseEvidence via ParseID at document\n+// admission with entry re-validation where a second entry reaches the\n+// same arm; New via the built-in constants. That test — not this comment\n+// — is the enforcement: it derives every BackendID site and every\n+// exported entry from production source, refuses hostile input through\n+// each entry without echo, fires each pair with a validated identity,\n+// and reports the validated/total ratio it measured.\n"}}}
