{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d29d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07a5e-8204-7c61-b778-7e703c0d991a"},"sequence":1961,"recorded_at":1780531400003917,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2a014316-3376-47a3-a185-8cb71122e6e6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"7bdb8133-6a12-4d06-a909-5bda097fe45c"},"task_id":"7bdb8133-6a12-4d06-a909-5bda097fe45c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"7bdb8133-6a12-4d06-a909-5bda097fe45c","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/conformance.go`.\n(436 line(s) above)\n437|func IdempotencyKey(operation string, segments ...string) (string, error) {\n438|\tparsedOperation, err := ParseOperation(operation)\n439|\tif err != nil {\n440|\t\treturn \"\", err\n441|\t}\n442|\tfor _, segment := range segments {\n443|\t\tif segment == \"\" {\n444|\t\t\treturn \"\", refuse(&Error{Code: CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"idempotency key shape\"})\n445|\t\t}\n446|\t}\n447|\twant := idempotencyKeySegments[parsedOperation]\n448|\tif want < 0 {\n449|\t\tif len(segments) < 1 {\n450|\t\t\treturn \"\", refuse(&Error{Code: CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"idempotency key shape\"})\n451|\t\t}\n452|\t} else if len(segments) != want {\n453|\t\treturn \"\", refuse(&Error{Code: CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"idempotency key shape\"})\n454|\t}\n455|\treturn strings.Join(segments, \"/\"), nil\n456|}\n457|\n458|// idempotencyKeySegments is the fixed per-operation segment count. status\n459|// carries its full queried identity tuple, so its count varies and only\n460|// the non-empty floor is enforced.\n461|var idempotencyKeySegments = map[Operation]int{\n462|\tOperationManifest: 1, OperationProbe: 1,\n463|\tOperationCreate: 2, OperationRestore: 2, OperationAttach: 2,\n464|\tOperationQuiesceInput: 3, OperationRequestStop: 3,\n465|\tOperationWaitSafeBoundary: 4, OperationTerminateStale: 4,\n466|\tOperationStatus: -1,\n467|}\n468|\n469|// Receipt is one durably bound idempotency record: the canonical key, the\n470|// operation it was bound for, and the recorded result identity. AX and the\n471|// backend bind the pair before the first child side effect (§4.1); an\n472|// identical retry returns the recorded result instead of acting again.\n473|type Receipt struct {\n474|\tKey       string\n475|\tOperation Operation\n476|\tResultID  string\n477|}\n478|\n479|// Ledger is the process-local idempotency receipt table backing the §4.C\n480|// recovery rules: persist the receipt before the first side effect,\n481|// identical retry replays it, a changed operation in the window is\n482|// idempotency_mismatch, and uncertainty requires status before any start\n483|// retry. The zero value is unusable; construct with NewLedger.\n484|//\n485|// The ledger is the semantic half of durability: Export and Import move\n486|// the table across a controller crash as stable bytes, and Import refuses\n487|// a malformed or ambiguous image instead of inventing an empty table.\n488|type Ledger struct {\n489|\tmutex    sync.Mutex\n490|\treceipts map[string]Receipt\n491|}\n492|\n493|// NewLedger opens an empty receipt table.\n494|func NewLedger() *Ledger {\n495|\treturn &Ledger{receipts: make(map[string]Receipt)}\n496|}\n(more lines below)"}}}
