ho + Error() render). Red-before: new test 6/6 FAIL; post-fix 7/7 PASS (exit 0).\\n- FINDING (census): all 31 BackendID-carrying refusal sites now validated — 27 in terminalbackend.go + 4 in manifest.go (probe arms via ParseProbe admission, manifest arms via ParseManifest admission + Resolve re-validation). Sibling packages measured, NOT changed (sibling suites pin their refusal text: secprim env_test asserts the echo verbatim): environ unknown-member echoes the full wire key (269B refusal, Error()-rendered, LIVE); secprim BuildEnv env-name echoes the full refused name (259B, LIVE); secprim paths truncate to 64 chars via memberErrorTarget (bounded, deliberate); secprim argv echoes positions only (clean); provhost Error() never echoes (static messages; identifiers travel in Details, inert + 16KiB ValidateDetails cap). The two LIVE sites are stated bounds with entry points, escaping content, and owner (sibling-suite pins) — follow-up leaves, not this diff.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-2okwyf_outcome-r2.md` + `battery_2okwyf_r2.json` (5 applied/5 killed/0 survived: narrowing 2 incl. length-gated + reorder, arm-deletion 1, census-only 1, audit-only 1 naming terminalbackend.go:651; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct rows; masks 15/243/665 all non-empty; mutant bodies in JSON). Round-1 battery anchors all still present (grep-verified); round-1 outcome/battery resources stand for unchanged code. Candidate tree OID in the outcome doc, detached-index write-tree AFTER the LOGBOOK append.\\n- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (all ok), `-race` terminalbackend exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (tb 95.1%, ph 86.0%, pv 97.8%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 0839 — 2okwyf: A5/A7/A8/A9/F-B1 closed (cross-package agreement, trust asymmetry, three nits, digit-guard sentence)\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-2okwyf, fourth leaf of STORY-260905-3t31e9. Production: `terminalbackend.go` (ParseID grammar arm drops BackendID echo; DigestFile §6.5/§7.1 asymmetry note), `provider.go` (trustCandidate §7.1/§6.5 mirror note), `provhost/probe.go` (decodeValidatedProbe single-decode split; RequireCapability consumes validated members), `provhost/protocol.go` (parseMajor leading-zero stated bound). Tests: new `provhost/profile_agreement_test.go` (order-sensitive cross-package equality), `TestParseIDGrammarRefusalEchoesNothing`, `TestParseMajorLeadingZeroIsClassifiedAsForeign`, `TestDecodeValidatedProbeHandsUsableMembersToRequireCapability`; one false sentence corrected in `digit_guard_census_test.go`.\\n- FINDING (A5 premise narrowed): a direct set-equality pin already exists (`TestSixProviderSetMatchesDiscoveryRegistry`, story-2 base) — the live hole was ORDER agreement only. Reorder mutant on either side alone leaves the whole old suite green and reddens only the new order pin (M-xprov-reorder: census 27 ran SURVIVED, behav 2 ran KILLED by the new test).\\n- FINDING (F-B1 sentence false as stated): pure named-const digit chain prunes silently — additive plant in `provhost/protocol.go` left both packages green (full suites) — while a mixed chain (named leaf + literal leaf) fails as unclassifiable (`mixes digit comparisons with unrelated comparisons`). First mixed probe passed vacuously on a wrong `-run` mask (matched only the unit test, census never ran); re-ran with `TestDigitCensusCoversEveryLeafGuard` non-empty. Sentence corrected to the precise split; absence re-verified by AST scan (0 digit-valued named constants, 0 such comparisons).\\n- FINDING (parseMajor strictness not free): rejecting leading zeros spells `== '0'`, which the digit-guard census rejects as unclassifiable (verified: strict mutant kills `TestDigitCensusCoversEveryLeafGuard` with ran=1 plus the provhost inventory with an unwitnessed parse arm) — so the bound close (classify-only, both arms refuse, gate admits exactly \\\"2.0.0\\\") is the correct one, pinned by `TestParseMajorLeadingZeroIsClassifiedAsForeign`.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-2okwyf_outcome.md` + `battery_2okwyf.json` (9 applied/9 killed/0 survived; narrowing 4, arm-deletion 2, census-only 1, audit-only 1 [leaf3 S-tb-shadow re-verified: census 15 + behav 229 SURVIVED, audit 658 KILLED naming conformance.go:713,:716], agreement 1; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct) attached as task resources. AC 4/4 rows driven. Candidate tree OID in the outcome doc, verified by `ls-tree` after every artifact write.\\n- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok, 0 FAIL), `-race` exit 0 (23 ok), `-cover` exit 0 (provhost 86.0%, provider 97.8%, terminalbackend 95.0%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok, catalog current, cigate contracts 6/6 + claims 6/6, fuzz smoke 13/13.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 0715 — v8heil round 2: site-recording seam closes the sibling-swallow class (F1/F2), all six findings fixed\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-v8heil rework (review rev2 CHANGES REQUESTED). Production seam in 4 files: `recordRefusal` hook (nil in prod) + `refuse` funnel (`//go:noinline`), hook calls in `mismatchf`/`integrityFailure`, 89 `&Error{}` literals routed through `refuse` same-line. Tests: new `refusal_site_audit_test.go` (TestMain exercised-line audit, row↔line mapping, skip pin, refuse-alias pins), line-carrying derivation with refuse-wrap enforcement, derived shadow-cover analysis replacing the 19 hand pairs, corrected N-R1 bound, dead loop deleted.\\n- FINDING (measured): pair-proves do not attribute — P8 plant left derivation identical + all 184 witnesses green; the audit kills it naming `conformance.go:713, :716`. The audit also caught a REAL pre-existing swallow on first run (`descriptor.go:123` never fired; #2 witness proved via sibling #1) — fixed as a witness (rename-away), not a bound.\\n- FINDING: clause sharing recomputed identically (62/184, 20 clauses, largest x11); death residual now 0/184. Stated remainder: rows bind to lines, witnesses do not (complementary swap invisible; shared with provider/provhost by construction).\\n- FINDING: F3's \\\"no strconv site\\\" was false — `provhost/opdecode.go rawUint53` exists, pinned by `count_overflow` (battery row B- reproduces the narrow-to-maxUint53+1 plant/kill).\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-v8heil_outcome-r2.md` + batteries (`battery_tb_r2` 8/8 incl. audit-only S-tb-shadow, `battery_ph_strconv` B-, re-ran core/pv/ph/x green; 19 applied/19 killed/0 survived + NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct) attached as task resources. Census: tb 210/210 lines (26 bound, 14 codes), ph 167/15, pv 18/3. AC 4/4 rows, refusals 369/395 driven + 26 bound. Candidate tree `9d7eaa4d…` verified by `ls-tree` + `hash-object` (11/11 MATCH).\\n- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok), `-race` exit 0 (23 ok), `-cover` exit 0 (70.2/86.0/97.8/95.0), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok, catalog current, cigate pass.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 0648 — v8heil: inventory machinery unified on invcore, tb ported to executed witnesses\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-v8heil. No production change (12 modified paths all `*_test.go`). New `internal/invcore` (ScanProduction/MustScanProduction, ParseBytes, DiffSets, ConstructorSpec+MustAuditConstructorReferences+WatchedCallPositions, SiteRecorder) + `terminalbackend/refusal_arm_witnesses_test.go` (184/210 arms executed at entry, 26 stated-bound rows pinned) + `TestQualifiedWatchesAdmitsPrefixSpellings` pin.\\n- FINDING (measured): provider records refusals at construction, so swallowing a built refusal downstream is census-invisible — D-pv mutant killed by the witness only, audit green. Execution-recorded, not outcome-recorded.\\n- FINDING: the `Errorf*` prefix stem had no pin (exact-`Errorf` plants passed without it); unit pin added, N-core-errorf-prefix kills through it.\\n- FINDING (harness): scoped `-run` silently skips provider's TestMain audit and early masks ran 0 tests in the wrong package — runner records ran-counts per mask and supports full-package census masks.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-v8heil_outcome.md` + `battery_v8heil.json` (15 applied/15 killed/0 survived + control rows; 9 census-only, 1 behav-only, 2 both, 3 provider-audit) attached as task resources. Census: tb 210=210, ph 167/15=167/15, pv 6/18/0/0=6/18/0/0. AC ratio 369/395 driven + 26 stated-bound. Candidate tree verified by `ls-tree` + `hash-object` (OID in the outcome doc).\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (23 pkgs, 0 FAIL), `-race` exit 0 (23 ok), `-cover` exit 0 (invcore 71.0%, provhost 86.0%, provider 97.8%, terminalbackend 94.9%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok, catalog current, cigate contracts pass.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 10182,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2546,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
